"""Original varied conversations; no templated substitution expansion."""
ROWS=[]
def add(family,group,*turns):ROWS.append(dict(family=family,group=group,turns=turns))
add('correction','correction_scope_suffix',
('My name is Alina Patel. The invitation calls me Alina Patil. Correct only the surname.','Alina Patel'),
('The host also wrote my guest’s name as Arun. That is correct.','Leave Arun unchanged; only your surname needs correcting.'),
('Write one message telling the host about it.','Could you change my surname from Patil to Patel on the invitation? Alina and my guest’s name, Arun, are already correct.'),
('Should both names now become Patel?','No. Patel is your surname correction. Arun’s name stays as it was.'))
add('correction','retry_without_new_fact',
('The notice says a meeting will happen next week, but no day is listed. Which day is it?','The notice does not provide a day, so I cannot determine it from that information.'),
('Try again. I really need a day.','I still do not have a day to give you. You could ask the organiser which day next week the meeting is scheduled for.'),
('I just found a second message saying Wednesday.','Then Wednesday is the day supported by the new message.'),
('Why could you answer after that but not before?','The second message supplied the missing day. Repeating the question alone did not add that information.'))
add('correction','polite_not_tentative',
('Make “Return the borrowed chairs by Friday” polite, but keep it a firm deadline.','Please return the borrowed chairs by Friday.'),
('Could we say “whenever you can”?','That would soften or remove the Friday deadline. If Friday is firm, keep it stated explicitly.'),
('Then add thanks without changing the deadline.','Please return the borrowed chairs by Friday. Thank you.'),
('Does please make Friday optional?','No. It makes the request polite while keeping Friday as the deadline.'),
('Give the final version with only one sentence.','Please return the borrowed chairs by Friday, thank you.'))
add('correction','uncertain_owner_revealed',
('A red umbrella was left in the cafe. I think it belongs to Noor, but I am not sure.','You can ask Noor whether it is theirs rather than state ownership as fact.'),
('Write that question.','Hi Noor, is the red umbrella left in the cafe yours?'),
('Noor replied no. We still do not know whose it is.','Noor has said it is not theirs; the owner remains unknown.'),
('The cafe manager later identified it as their own.','The cafe manager has now identified the umbrella as theirs.'),
('Should my earlier guess about Noor stay in the final found-property note?','No. The later identification supersedes that guess.'))
add('correction','report_firsthand_revision',
('Write: I saw the fence fall during the storm.','I saw the fence fall during the storm.'),
('Actually I saw it lying down afterwards. I did not see it fall.','I saw the fence lying down after the storm.'),
('Could I still say the storm definitely knocked it over?','Not from that observation alone. Seeing it down afterwards does not establish exactly how it fell.'),
('Write a cautious note to the owner.','I noticed the fence was down after the storm. I did not see it fall, so I do not know exactly what happened.'))
add('correction','interrupted_plan_resume',
('Help me plan a quiet afternoon at home: reading first, then a film.','Start with reading, then watch a film when you are ready to switch activities.'),
('Before that, how do I politely decline a phone call right now?','You could say, “I cannot talk right now. Could we arrange another time?”'),
('Thanks. Back to the afternoon: swap the order.','Watch the film first, then read.'),
('The order of what? Just checking that we did not swap anything about the phone call.','The afternoon activities: film before reading. The phone-call message is a separate task.'),
('Make the plan one short line.','Film first, reading afterwards.'))
add('correction','sibling_perspective_switch',
('Write a note from me to my sister: I will collect your suitcase tomorrow.','I will collect your suitcase tomorrow.'),
('Now write her reply agreeing, from her point of view.','That works for me. You can collect my suitcase tomorrow.'),
('In her reply, whose suitcase is “my suitcase”?','Your sister’s suitcase, because the reply is written from her point of view.'),
('Change the collection day to Sunday in both messages.','Your message: “I will collect your suitcase on Sunday.”\nHer reply: “That works for me. You can collect my suitcase on Sunday.”'))
add('correction','permission_limited_channel',
('I told the club they could share my poem in the printed booklet, but not on social media.','Your permission covers the printed booklet only, not social media.'),
('I now also allow their email newsletter. Social media is still excluded.','The allowed uses are the printed booklet and email newsletter. Social media remains excluded.'),
('Give me a short message confirming that.','You may share my poem in the printed booklet and email newsletter, but please do not post it on social media.'),
('Someone says allowing email means allowing all online use.','That is broader than the permission you gave. You specifically added the email newsletter while keeping social media excluded.'),
('What changed from my first permission?','You added the email newsletter; the printed booklet was already allowed.'))
add('memory','audio_story_spoiler',
('My friend has heard only the first episode of my audio story. In a message to them, do not reveal that the narrator is the missing brother.','I will keep that reveal out of the message to your friend.'),
('Ask what they thought of the opening scene by the river.','What did you think of the opening scene by the river?'),
('I also want to know whether the music was too loud.','What did you think of the opening scene by the river? Was the music too loud?'),
('The friend says the atmosphere was good but some words were hard to hear.','You could thank them and ask where the words became unclear, without assuming whether the music or the voice recording caused it.'),
('Write that follow-up.','Thanks, that is helpful. Can you tell me where the words became hard to hear?'),
('Should I add “Did you guess he was the missing brother?”','No. That question would reveal the identity you asked to keep out of the message.'),
('Which episode has my friend heard?','Only the first episode.'))
add('memory','quiet_cafe_preference',
('I am choosing a place to read. Quiet matters more to me than fashionable decor, and I do not need Wi-Fi.','Look for somewhere quiet with a comfortable place to sit. Decor and Wi-Fi can stay secondary to the reading atmosphere you want.'),
('One cafe has plain furniture and no background music. Another looks beautiful but has a live band.','From those descriptions, the plain cafe without music fits your priority better than the cafe with a live band.'),
('I might bring a paper notebook to jot down ideas.','That fits a reading visit without relying on Wi-Fi.'),
('Give me a gentle reminder to stop checking my phone.','Let the book have your attention for a while.'),
('Help me ask whether it is okay to sit and read while I have a drink.','Would it be okay for me to sit and read for a while with my drink?'),
('The quieter cafe has no Wi-Fi. Does that disqualify it under my original request?','No. You said you do not need Wi-Fi.'))
add('memory','translation_names_fixed',
('I am simplifying a paragraph for English learners. Keep the names Aditi and Omar exactly as they are.','I will simplify the wording without changing Aditi or Omar.'),
('Here is the paragraph: Aditi postponed the visit because Omar was unavailable.','Aditi delayed the visit because Omar was not available.'),
('Can postponed mean cancelled forever?','No. It means moved to a later time, not necessarily cancelled.'),
('Use that distinction to explain the sentence briefly.','Aditi moved the visit to a later time because Omar was not available. It does not say the visit was cancelled altogether.'),
('Make it even simpler, but do not change who was unavailable.','Aditi moved the visit to a later time because Omar could not be there.'),
('Would replacing the names with common English names make it easier?','It might make the names more familiar to some readers, but it would break your instruction to keep Aditi and Omar unchanged.'),
('Who was unable to be there?','Omar.'))
add('memory','garden_seed_swap_pending',
('I offered basil seeds in exchange for Priya’s marigold seeds. She has not accepted yet.','You have proposed a swap, but it is not agreed yet.'),
('I need a label for my envelope.','Basil seeds'),
('Should I put Priya’s name on it as if it already belongs to her?','You can set it aside for the proposed swap, but you should not treat the exchange as completed before she agrees.'),
('Help me ask whether she is interested without pushing.','Would you be interested in swapping some marigold seeds for my basil seeds? No problem if not.'),
('She says she has already given away the marigolds.','Then the proposed swap cannot go ahead as described, unless she offers something else and you agree.'),
('Have I received any seeds from her?','You have not said that you received any.'),
('Which seeds are in my envelope?','Basil seeds.'))
add('memory','short_story_unreliable_narrator',
('In my story, the narrator believes the empty house is abandoned. The author’s plan is that someone still lives there. Keep belief and reality separate.','The narrator can describe signs that make the house seem abandoned, but their belief should not be presented as proof that no one lives there.'),
('Write one sentence from the narrator’s limited point of view.','With the curtains drawn and the garden overgrown, I assumed no one lived there anymore.'),
('I want the reader to have a small reason to doubt that assumption.','You could mention a small sign of recent activity, such as a freshly watered plant by the door, without explaining who watered it.'),
('Use that. Keep it subtle.','Beside the door, one pot held damp soil, though the rest of the garden looked dry.'),
('Can the narrator still be mistaken at this point?','Yes. The narrator still believes the house is abandoned, while the new detail gives the reader a reason to question that belief.'),
('What is true in my underlying story plan?','Someone still lives in the house.'),
('Have we named that person?','No. The resident has not been named.'))
add('memory','shared_oven_schedule',
('In our flat, I booked the oven for the first hour after six, and Eli booked the following hour. We agreed not to overlap.','Your oven slot comes first, starting at six; Eli’s follows it. The slots should stay separate.'),
('I want to prepare my tray beforehand so I do not run late.','You could have the tray ready before your slot begins and leave time to remove it before Eli’s slot.'),
('Write Eli a message asking whether they need the kitchen counter too.','Will you need the kitchen counter during your oven slot as well?'),
('No reply yet. I will not assume the counter is free.','That keeps the counter question open until Eli replies.'),
('A friend suggests I leave my food in through Eli’s hour. Would that fit our agreement?','No. You agreed not to overlap oven use, so leaving your food in during Eli’s slot would conflict with that.'),
('Does booking the oven also tell us who has the counter?','No. The counter use has not been agreed from what you shared.'),
('Who has the oven slot immediately after mine?','Eli.'))
add('memory','workshop_observer_role',
('I am attending a pottery workshop as an observer. I have not booked a place to use the wheel.','Your place is for observing, not using the wheel.'),
('I would like to take notes, if the organiser allows it.','You can ask whether note-taking is allowed for observers.'),
('Draft that question and ask where observers should sit.','May observers take notes, and where should we sit?'),
('The organiser says notes are fine and observers should use the back row.','You can take notes and sit in the back row under that instruction.'),
('Does that reply give me a turn on the wheel?','No. It addresses notes and seating, not changing your observer place into a practical place.'),
('If I want to try the wheel, what should I ask instead?','Ask whether a practical place is available and what you would need to do to book it.'),
('What permission has actually been confirmed?','You may take notes, and observers should sit in the back row.'))
add('memory','family_recipe_credit',
('This soup recipe came from my grandfather. My aunt taught me to make it. I want to credit both roles accurately.','You can say the recipe came from your grandfather and that your aunt taught you how to make it.'),
('I changed the seasoning a little. Do not call the whole recipe my invention.','You can describe it as your version of your grandfather’s recipe, with seasoning adjusted by you.'),
('I want to let my friends know dinner is ready, without a speech about the recipe.','The soup is ready. Come and help yourselves!'),
('Can that sound a little gentler?','The soup is ready whenever you would like some.'),
('Who should get credit for teaching me, rather than originating the recipe?','Your aunt.'))
